UncitedCommentDefaultMessage=Uncited references: This section comprises references that occur in the reference list but not in the body of the text. Please position each reference in the text or, alternatively, delete it. Any reference not dealt with will be retained in this section. Thank you.
UncitedCommentWithRefInMessage=Uncited reference: %s is not cited in text; please indicate where a citation should appear or delete it from the reference list.
UnlistedCommentDefaultMessage=The following citation \"%s\" is unlisted.
UnlistedCommentWithRefInMessage=Missing reference: %s is not listed in the \u2018References\u2019 section; please provide complete reference details.
authorDegreeShouldBePresent=Please provide professional degrees (e.g., PhD, MD) for the author%s \"%s\".
MandatoryProfessionalTitleMessage=Please provide Professional job titles (e.g., Professor, Asst Professor) for the author%s \"%s\" as it is mandatory as per journal style.
authorDegreeMissingForFewAuthors=Please provide no more than two qualifications for the author%s \"%s\".
SectionaHeadings=As per journal style, all %s should ONLY have the following numbered first level section headings: %s. Please check and amend accordingly.
checkForCharstyleThatAreMandatoryHighlight=Check for the existence of pagination in the citation. If not, raise an author query.
checkForCharstyleThatAreMandatory=Please provide the %s for the reference %s.
addAOrBInYearInRefList=The year in the %s occurrence of %s in the list has been changed to %s.
AbstractWordCount=%s is not provided in the correct format. Please correct the format based on the following specification: %s %s should not exceed more than %s words. %s
checkForCharstyleThatAreMandatoryMFC=Please provide the volume number or issue number or page range for the bibliography in Ref(s). %s
checkForCharstyleThatAreMandatoryMFC_altno=Please provide the volume number, issue number, page range (or article number) for the bibliography in Ref(s). %s
StructuredAbstract=As per journal style, \u2018Abstract\u2019 should be structured and should have the following 5 headings: Objectives, Design, Methods, Results and Conclusions. Please check and provide the same.
UnstructuredAbstract=As per journal style, the subheads and casing of Structured abstract should be as follows: Background/Aims, Methods, Results, Conclusion. Please check and take appropriate action.
StandardizedAbstract=Abstract subheadings should be 'Purpose, Materials and Methods, Results, Conclusions'. Please check.
StandardizedAbstractWithMethods=Abstract subheadings should be 'Purpose, Methods, Results, Conclusions'. Please check.
missingMiddleInit=As per style, author names in the author group must have First name/Middle Initial/Surname, i.e. Marc D. Feldman. Please check and provide the complete names for the author(s) \"%s\".
ExpWithDiffAbbre=The definition \"%s\" has been abbreviated as \"%s\" as well as \"%s\". Please check if the representation should be made consistent in the article.
highlightSectionOrder=Order of highlights should be \"abstractauthorhighlights\" and \"abstracteditorhighlights\"
charCountQuery=Highlights should only consist of \"%s\" characters per bullet point, including spaces. The highlights provided are too long; please edit them to meet the requirement.%s
charCountQueryForcellpress=Journal guidelines limit each highlight to \"%s\" characters or fewer, including spaces. Could you please let me know how to modify the highlights below so that they fit within this guideline? (Please note that the text below may differ from what you had previously submitted as a result of editorial revisions.)
BulletlistQuery=Highlights should consist of 3 to 5 bullet points. There are \"%s\" bullet points provided. Please edit the highlights to meet the requirement.
BulletlistQueryMax4= Highlights should consist of a maximum of 4 bullet points. There are \"%s\" bullet points provided. Please edit the highlights to meet the requirement.
highlightForLabel=Highlights should be a short collection of bullet points. Insert bullet as label.
roleAndDegreeMandatory=As per style, roles and degrees of corresponding author should be retained in the correspondence field. Please check and raise an author query.
queryForAbbWithTwoExpansion=Please note that both %s and %s have been abbreviated to %s. Kindly differentiate between the two binomials throughout the article.
queryForAbbWithThreeExpansion=Please note that %s, %s and %s have been abbreviated to %s. Kindly differentiate between the three binomials throughout the article.
queryForAbbWithFourExpansion=Please note that %s, %s, %s and %s have been abbreviated to %s. Kindly differentiate between the four binomials throughout the article.
ISSN-highlightWordsNotInDBWithDot=The corresponding abbreviation for this word is not found in the ISSN database. Hence, check and abbreviate this word in title case with a dot.
ISSN-highlightWordsNotInDBWithoutDot=The corresponding abbreviation for this word is not found in the ISSN database. Hence, check and abbreviate this word in title case without a dot.
SuggestionForMissingCorrAddress=Note that there are more than one corresponding author and the correspondence address is not given. Please check and query the author.
highlightIdenticalAffiliation=This affiliation is a duplicate of affiliation \"%s\". Please delete this and change the citations accordingly.
FirstAuConsideredAsCorresAuComment=The first author has been considered as the corresponding author. Please verify.
CorresAuObtainedFromCoverSheet="%s" has been considered as the corresponding author as per the coversheet. Please verify.
AffNotInSequence=Affiliation designators '%s' provided but the corresponding affiliation is missing. Kindly check and action accordingly.
insertCommentForMissingCorresPara=Create a correspondingauthor parastyle with label %s and bookmark %s with email: as content 
insertQueryIfRefIsCitedOnlyInAbstractAndNotElsewhereInTheFile=The reference \"%s\" is cited only in the abstract and not in the text. Please introduce a citation in the text.
insertQueryIfRefIsCitedOnlyInAbstractAndDeleteCitedRef=This reference citation is also cited in text. Hence, per style, remove it from abstract and reword the sentence accordingly.
queryFormismatchSectionAHeadings=As per journal style, only fixed headings (1. Introduction, 2. Materials and Supplies, 3. Detailed Methods, 4. Potential Pitfalls and Trouble Shooting) are allowed. Please check and amend as necessary.
wordCountInFullArticle=Note that the word count limit exceeds 4500 words. Refer the style sheet and proceed accordingly.
journalExpansionHighlightText=This journal title does not directly match with the abbreviation/expansion in Index Medicus DB. Please check and if appropriate, replace with the below expansion(s) \"%s\", which has been obtained under the search criteria \"%s\".
journalMultipleExpansionHighlightText=For this journal title, the following expansions \'%s\' match closely in the Index Medius DB. Check and use the appropriate expansion.
generalSuggestion=This journal title is not found in Index Medicus DB. Please check and use the correct expansion.
standardTextInLRH=Short title should be in sentence case. Please check.
CasingSuggestionForLowerCaseReplace=Change to lowercase if appropriate.
DefaultSuggestionForMRW=Article title should be in title case. First word, nouns, pronouns, adjectives, verbs, and subordinate conjunctions should be capitalized. Lowercase articles, coordinate conjunctions (and, or, for, nor), and all prepositions, unless they are the first or last words of the title. Lowercase the \"to\" in infinitives.
CasingSuggestionIntoLowerCaseAfterEmDashEndashColon=Change the word after colon/emdash/spaced endash to lowercase if appropriate.
CasingSuggestionForSentenceCase=Change to sentence case if appropriate.
CasingSuggestionForTitleCase=Change to title case if appropriate.
CasingSuggestionForUpperCase=Change to upper case if appropriate.
checkIfAbbreviationOrPrepositionWithDotMessage=(1) Delete if this is a preposition/conjunction and (2) add a dot if an abbreviation.
checkIfAbbreviationOrPrepositionWithoutDotMessage=(1) Delete if this is a preposition/conjunction and (2) remove dot if an abbreviation.
checkIfAbbreviationOrPrepositionMessage=Delete if this is a preposition/conjunction
missingreflabels=References are not in sequence. Please check
COIDefaultStatementNoAuChk=No benefits in any form have been received or will be received from a commercial party related directly or indirectly to the subject of this article.
commentAllAuFootnote=Insert the standard statement ['All authors have none to declare.'] as paragraph with 'Conflicts of interest' as 'sectiona' if all authors have no conflict of interest.
commentSingleAuFootnote=Insert the standard statement ['The author has none to declare.'] as paragraph with 'Conflicts of interest' as 'sectiona' if the author has no conflict of interest.
commentNoAuChkFootnote=Insert the standard statement ['No benefits in any form have been received or will be received from a commercial party related directly or indirectly to the subject of this article.'] as paragraph with 'Conflicts of interest' as 'sectiona' if the author(s) has/have no conflict of interest.
commentForDrugDosage=If there are any drug dosages in your article, please verify them and indicate that you have done so by initialing this query.
CasingSuggestionForLowerCaseReplaceInReference=Change to lowercase if appropriate.
commentForSectionNumbering=In sentence beginning \u201C_______\,\u201D please confirm that \u201C%s %s\u201D refers to %s.
highlightCommentForSectionNumbering=Replace \'%s %s%s\' with the respective section/subsection citation and query the author to check.
highlightCommentToChangeInitialsInAck=If this represents the initials of the author, then it should appear closed up with dots, e.g., D.A.W.
highlightCommentForWhiteSquare=As per MFC, open square present at the end of enunciation is allowed. Follow author usage and do not delete.
highlightCommentForwithoutWhiteSquare=As per MFC, open square present at the end of enunciation is allowed if the author provides (follow author). Check for missing open square in the manuscript and insert if present.
unlistedVettedDegree=Degree abbreviations are verified against a list of known degrees. %s %s not yet on this list. Please verify these degrees.
highlightCommentForMissingEqnLink=Equations are numbered according to the Appendix designation: (A1), (A2), ... for those in the first appendix section; (B1), (B2) ...  for the second; (C1), (C2), ... for those in the third, etc. Equation '%s' is not cited in text. Check and raise an author query.
highlightCommentForMissingEqnLabel=Equations are numbered according to the Appendix designation: (A1), (A2), ... for those in the first appendix section; (B1), (B2) ...  for the second; (C1), (C2), ... for those in the third, etc. Equation '%s' is cited in text but its equation is missing. Check and raise an author query.
highlightCommentForSetRanges=Ranges should be set as, eg, Eqs. (A1)-(A3) (ndash) in the middle of a sentence and Equations (A1)-(A3) in the beginning of a sentence, with the equations numbered according to the Appendix designation: (A1), (A2), ... for those in the first appendix section; (B1), (B2) ...  for the second; (C1), (C2), ... for those in the third, etc.
highlightCommentForSetRangesForEquations=Ranges should be set as, eg, Eqs. (A1)-(A3) (ndash) if abbreviated and Equations (A1)-(A3) if expanded, with the equations numbered according to the Appendix designation: (A1), (A2), ... for those in the first appendix section; (B1), (B2) ...  for the second; (C1), (C2), ... for those in the third, etc.
insertQueryIfAccessDateMissing=CE: Please provide complete accessed date in Ref(s). %s.
standardArticleFootnoteText=Inclusion of any material in this section does not imply endorsement by the Society for Nutrition Education and Behavior. Evaluative comments contained in the reviews reflect the views of the authors. Review abstracts are either prepared by the reviewer or extracted from the product literature. Prices quoted are those provided by the publishers at the time materials were submitted. They may not be current when the review is published. Reviewers receive a complimentary copy of the resource as part of the review process.
AbstractGraphicalGrtThan250=The first line of the Abstract has been inserted as the Graphical Abstract text; however, it currently exceeds the space available for the published version. Please check that the text is suitable and trim it so that it is less than 250 characters (including spaces).
AbstractGraphicallessThan250=Please check that the inserted Graphical Abstract text is suitable. Please ensure that the text is no longer than 250 characters (including spaces).
AbstractGraphicalntEqGrtThan250=The Graphical Abstract text currently exceeds the space available for the published version. Please trim the text so that it is less than 250 characters (including spaces).
