mandatoryHeadingOfAbstractSubheads=Please note that as per style the abstract should include the following mandatory headings: Purpose; Design/methodology/approach; Findings; Originality/value. Hence, please provide content for the subheading(s) \"%s\".
rearrangeAbstractHeadingOrder=As per journal style, the subheads and casing of Structured abstract should be as follows: Purpose; Design/methodology/approach; Findings; Originality/value. Please check and take appropriate action.
uncitedCommentForFurtherReading_2=Reference(s) that is/are not cited in the text is/are moved to the \u0022Further reading\u0022 section. Please check.
SuggestionForMismatchInStandardText=The provided box content does not match with the standard text provided for box. Please check and make the necessary changes.
StandardTextForCRP=This Short Case is brought to you in association with the Pathological Society of Great Britain and Ireland. Each month we feature a Short Case written by a member of the Trainees\u2019 Subcommittee of the Pathological Society of Great Britain and Ireland. This case, including its scanned slides, is published on the Pathological Society\u2019s website %s (previous cases can be accessed by members via the education portal login). The Short Case includes a series of Test Yourself Questions at the end to check your understanding of the case. We hope you enjoy reading it.%s
